<article class="env-lemma" id="0GB2">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0GB2">Lemma <span data-tag="0GB2">88.8.6</span>.</a> Let $A_1 \to A_2$ be a map of Noetherian rings. Let $I_ i \subset A_ i$ be an ideal such that $V(I_1A_2) = V(I_2)$. Let $B_1$ be in (<a href="/tag/0AL4" data-tag="0AL4">88.2.0.2</a>) for $(A_1, I_1)$. Let $B_2$ be the base change of $B_1$ as in Remark <a href="/tag/0AL5" data-tag="0AL5">88.2.3</a>. If $B_1$ is rig-étale over $(A_1, I_1)$, then $B_2$ is rig-étale over $(A_2, I_2)$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Follows from Lemma <a href="/tag/0AK2" data-tag="0AK2">88.8.5</a> and Definition <a href="/tag/0GAY" data-tag="0GAY">88.8.1</a> and the fact that $I_2^ c \subset I_1A_2$ for some $c \geq 0$ as $A_2$ is Noetherian. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>